{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/news/michael-dugher-appointed-as-music-champion","content_id":"177f1b11-880d-4825-afb1-068aabb27a67","description":"As outlined in the publication of Turn It Up: Our Plan for Music, the Secretary of State for the Department for Culture, Media and Sport has appointed Michael Dugher as a Music Champion","details":{"attachments":[],"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><h2 id=\"bmichael-dugherb\"><b>Michael Dugher<b></b></b></h2>\n\n<p>The Secretary of State for Culture, Media and Sport is delighted to announce the appointment of Michael Dugher as the government’s Music Champion. The Music Champion will support the government’s new Plan for Music (<a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/turn-it-up-our-plan-for-music/\">Turn it Up: Our Plan for Music</a>), and act as an advocate for the sector. Commencing on 13 July 2026, this will be a year-long unremunerated appointment, with the opportunity for extension at the end of the term. </p>\n\n<p>A lifelong music fan and campaigner, Michael will bring a wealth of knowledge to the role, with over three decades working in leadership roles across both government and industry. Michael was a Member of Parliament from 2010-2017, during which time he held a number of senior positions including as Shadow Secretary of State for Culture, Media &amp; Sport. Prior to this, he held multiple senior roles in government as a special advisor, including as Chief Political Spokesman for the then-Prime Minister, Gordon Brown.</p>\n\n<p>After standing down from Parliament, Michael became the CEO of UK Music, where he spent three years working with a wide range of organisations to represent, support and advocate for the sector. Michael was also a member of the Creative Industries Council. In 2018, in recognition for his services to music, he was awarded a Fellowship at the Leeds Conservatoire (formerly the Leeds College of Music). Michael was also previously a Board member for the Ivors Academy Trust. </p>\n\n<p>In this new role, Michael will act as a conduit between government and the sector to increase the reach of the government’s new Plan for Music, and identify further opportunities to support and grow the sector.</p>\n\n<p>See also: <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/guidance/music-champion-terms-of-reference\">Music Champion - Terms of reference</a>.</p>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-07-13T16:00:00Z"}],"emphasised_organisations":["ae9ef2e1-9de0-4ff8-b560-e6ac28a6205c"],"images":[{"caption":null,"content_type":"image/jpeg","sources":{"s216":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e59279b86650c53b2cefbfe/placeholder.jpg","s300":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e59279b86650c53b2cefbfe/placeholder.jpg","s465":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e59279b86650c53b2cefbfe/placeholder.jpg","s630":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e59279b86650c53b2cefbfe/placeholder.jpg","s712":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e59279b86650c53b2cefbfe/placeholder.jpg","s960":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e59279b86650c53b2cefbfe/placeholder.jpg"},"type":"lead"}],"political":true},"document_type":"press_release","first_published_at":"2026-07-13T17:00:00+01:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/news/michael-dugher-appointed-as-music-champion","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/news/michael-dugher-appointed-as-music-champion","base_path":"/government/news/michael-dugher-appointed-as-music-champion","content_id":"177f1b11-880d-4825-afb1-068aabb27a67","document_type":"press_release","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-07-13T16:00:00Z","schema_name":"news_article","title":"Michael Dugher appointed as Music Champion","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/news/michael-dugher-appointed-as-music-champion","withdrawn":false}],"emphasised_organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"